  "summary": "Full assessment of all 318 Chinese/Vietnamese passages in nine chapters, the chapter titles, the dateline and both titles, by two separate-context assessors who each read every pair in their half and checked consistency across the two drafting parts. The mock preface, the spiritual victories, the little nun and Wu Ma, A Q’s decline, his return from town, the revolution, the robbery, the trial and the execution are complete, with Lu Xun’s irony and the recurring formulas intact. The assessors scored the halves 8.925 and 8.85 with no major findings; the register, consistency and fidelity issues they reported were revised. Fidelity, voice, imagery and mechanics are 9.0, naturalness 8.5. Unrounded weighted score 8.925 meets the unchanged 8.6 threshold. No unresolved major or critical issue remains.",
